#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""board-sweep (sf#1338): clear the board's blocked inbox by fixed rules.

Usage: board-sweep [--apply] [--base-url URL] [--forge-url URL]

Env: PAPERCLIP_API_URL (or --base-url), PAPERCLIP_API_KEY (header only),
  PAPERCLIP_COMPANY_ID, FORGEJO_TOKEN (header only), FORGEJO_API_URL (or
  --forge-url); optional PAPERCLIP_RUN_ID, sent on every write as
  X-Paperclip-Run-Id the way fleet/bin/board-link sends it.

Default is a DRY RUN: every action is computed and printed, nothing is written.
--apply performs the writes. A write is a comment
`board-sweep: <action> -- <reason>` on the issue, then the status PATCH; a
status never changes without its comment first.

Rules, first match wins, for every blocked issue:
  1. nagatha       assigned to Nagatha: never touched.
  2. review        `Review <owner/repo>#<n> @ <sha>` (and the reviewer sub-task
                   shapes): cancelled when the PR is closed, merged, or its
                   head moved; kickback when a required check failed or the
                   lead's verdict is fix-first (below);
                   otherwise, per exact title, the newest is a todo candidate
                   for the priority queue and older ones are cancelled.
  3. merge-check   `Checks not green ...` / `Resolve merge-check read failure
                   ...`: cancelled when the PR is not open, else listed.
  4. routine       routine_execution: one open instance per routine survives,
                   the newest; other blocked instances are cancelled. A newest
                   instance that is blocked is listed as routine-kept.
  5. parent        every child terminal and every first-class blockedBy
                   dependency done (SOF-10842): back to todo. List rows omit
                   blockedBy, so the candidate's issue detail is read; a
                   failed read or a detail without a blockedBy list is an
                   error and the task stays as it is (fail closed). A
                   blocker in any status but done (cancelled included)
                   keeps it blocked, listed as other.
  6. waiting-author `Triage <owner/repo>#<n>` (sf#1366): cancelled when the
                   Forge issue is closed; back to todo when the issue's author
                   commented after the board issue's updatedAt; otherwise
                   listed as waiting-author, unchanged.
  7. other         listed, unchanged.

Review tasks in todo or in_progress (The operator, 2026-10-04: stalled reviews get
kickstarted unless invalid, then kicked back; the most important first):
  - invalid        PR closed/merged or head moved: cancel. A required check
                   (factory/smoke, factory/prepush) failure|error at the
                   reviewed sha: kickback = one `REVIEW KICKBACK:` comment on
                   the Forge PR per sha, then the task cancelled unless it
                   carries counted fix-first evidence (its status is kept). Blocked
                   reviews get the same kickback. So does a lead verdict of
                   fix-first at the reviewed sha (sf#1813): the newest board
                   comment by a lead (Adams, Czajka, Smythe) carrying
                   `## Review of <repo>#<n> at <sha7>` and a `verdict:` line,
                   read from every task of that PR and sha7, any status.
  - kickstart      updatedAt older than BOARD_SWEEP_STALL_MIN minutes (default
                   30, against BOARD_SWEEP_NOW or the clock) and no queued or
                   running run in the task's own runs list: comment, then
                   todo, which wakes the assignee. A todo the board refuses
                   adds a `board-sweep: kickstart-refused` comment.
  - escalate       stalled again after two earlier kickstarts the board
                   accepted (refused ones do not count): one comment and
                   one high-priority `Stalled review: <title>` issue for
                   Bishop, unless one is already open. Never the operator.
Queue: every todo candidate (kickstarts and blocked-review releases) is
ordered by priority (critical, high, medium, low), then the lowest `pri:N`
label (unlabelled last), then oldest createdAt. Each assignee takes at most
its free slots (maxConcurrentRuns minus its queued+running runs from
live-runs; 1 when the agent states none; a full 50-row live-runs page counts
as 50 for every assignee); an assignee with no free slot still takes its first
kickstart. Admitted writes go out in queue order. The rest stay as they are,
listed as review-next-pass `queued: priority <p>, position <k>`. A failed
live-runs or task-runs read holds every kickstart and release this sweep.

The per-run cross-issue write cap (SOF-10747): the board allows one heartbeat
run 20 cross-issue comments plus status updates, then answers 429 with
details.code `cross_issue_influence_cap_exceeded`. Every item that writes is
handled in priority order (critical, high, medium, low, then the lowest
`pri:N`, then within one priority cleanups before releases, then oldest)
within a budget of BOARD_SWEEP_MAX_WRITES board issue writes (default 18;
every request to /api/issues/... counts, retries included). An item starts
only when its writes fit (2; a kickstart 3, room for its refusal note; an
escalation 1). The first item that does not fit, or the first cap 429, stops
all writes at once: that write is not retried, and it and every later item
that writes is listed as `next-pass` with `planned: <action>` (and `partial`
when some of its writes went out, naming `the cap` or `the write budget ran
out`). A retry also keeps room for the rest of its item (SOF-10912): a
comment is retried only while the budget still holds its status PATCH, so
no comment is accepted without room for its status write; a kickstart PATCH
the budget stops still posts its refusal note, from its reserved write.
That is not an error: the JSON still
prints, `stopped` names the reason, and the next hourly pass takes the rest.
A dry run previews the same budget.

Writes are paced, at most one per BOARD_SWEEP_WRITE_GAP_MS (default 200). A
write answered 503, or 429 without the cap code, is retried, up to 5
attempts, waiting Retry-After (capped at 30 s) or 1, 2, 4, 8 s. A failed
write records its HTTP status and reason. A 422 on the todo PATCH (the board refuses todo, e.g. open blockedBy
issues) is a skip, not an error. BOARD_SWEEP_NO_WAIT=1 makes every wait
zero-length (tests).

Output: one JSON object (mode, blocked_before, actions, errors, error_codes,
skipped, write_budget, writes (board issue writes sent), stopped (null or why
writes stopped), items, queue (first 20 waiting), and blocked_after in apply
mode). Exit: 0 clean | 1 errors > 0
or a board read failed | 2 bad argument | 3 missing environment (nothing sent).
"""
import datetime
import json
import os
import re
import runpy
from pathlib import Path
import sys
import subprocess
import time
import urllib.error
import urllib.parse
import urllib.request

TERMINAL = {"done", "cancelled"}
NAGATHA = "Nagatha"
PAGE = 500
MAX_PAGES = 100
# The lead's review and every reviewer sub-task: "Review", "Adams: blind
# review", "Chang: blind senior shadow review", "Chang review", "Blind review".
REVIEW = re.compile(
    r"^(?:[A-Za-z]+:? )?(?:[Bb]lind )?(?:(?:senior|junior) )?(?:shadow )?[Rr]eview "
    r"(\S+/\S+)#(\d+) @ ([0-9a-f]{7,40})"
)
FOLLOW_UP = re.compile(r"^(?:Checks not green|Resolve merge-check read failure)\b.*?(\S+/\S+)#(\d+)")
EXEMPT = re.compile(r"^\s*(?:triage|review|merge|write spec|spec-writing|diagnose|research|audit|run-audit|fleet audit|infra:|ask:|backlog:|config:)(?:\b|\s)", re.I)
TRIAGE = re.compile(r"^Triage (\S+/\S+)#(\d+)$")
ACTIONS = ["cancel", "todo", "kickback", "kickstart", "escalate", "nagatha", "merge-check",
           "routine-kept", "queue", "review-next-pass", "waiting-author", "other", "next-pass"]
REQUIRED_CHECKS = ("factory/smoke", "factory/prepush")
PRIORITY = ["critical", "high", "medium", "low"]
PRI_LABEL = re.compile(r"^pri:(\d+)$")
ACTIVE_RUN = {"queued", "running"}
ESCALATE_TO = "Bishop"
KICKSTART = "board-sweep: kickstart"
KICKSTART_REFUSED = "board-sweep: kickstart-refused"
KICKSTARTS_BEFORE_ESCALATE = 2
LIVE_RUNS_CAP = 50
QUEUE_SHOWN = 20
RETRY_STATUS = {429, 503}
ATTEMPTS = 5
RETRY_AFTER_CAP = 30
CAP_CODE = "cross_issue_influence_cap_exceeded"
MAX_WRITES = 18  # the board's per-run cap is 20 (paperclipai 2026.916.1)
ISSUE_WRITE = "/api/issues/"  # the writes the cap counts: comments and updates
# Board issue writes each action needs; a kickstart keeps room for its refusal note.
COST = {"cancel": 2, "todo": 2, "kickback": 2, "queue": 2, "kickstart": 3, "escalate": 1}


def die(msg, code=1):
    sys.stderr.write(f"board-sweep: {msg}\n")
    sys.exit(code)


class Http:
    def __init__(self, base, auth, run_id=""):
        self.base, self.auth, self.run_id = base, auth, run_id

    def call(self, method, path, body=None):
        headers = {"Authorization": self.auth, "Accept": "application/json"}
        data = None
        if body is not None:
            data = json.dumps(body).encode()
            headers["Content-Type"] = "application/json"
            if self.run_id:
                headers["X-Paperclip-Run-Id"] = self.run_id
        req = urllib.request.Request(self.base + path, data=data, headers=headers, method=method)
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=30) as r:
            raw = r.read().decode()
            return json.loads(raw) if raw.strip() else None


class Stop(BaseException):
    """Stop every write this pass: the budget is spent or the board's cap was hit.
    A BaseException, so the per-write `except Exception` handlers never swallow it.
    `kind` is "budget" or "cap", so a partial item says which one stopped it."""

    def __init__(self, msg, kind):
        super().__init__(msg)
        self.kind = kind


def http_body(e):
    """An HTTPError's response body, read once and kept, so two readers agree."""
    if not hasattr(e, "sweep_body"):
        try:
            e.sweep_body = e.read().decode(errors="replace")
        except Exception:
            e.sweep_body = ""
    return e.sweep_body


def is_cap(e):
    """True for the board's per-run cross-issue write cap refusal."""
    if not (isinstance(e, urllib.error.HTTPError) and e.code == 429):
        return False
    try:
        doc = json.loads(http_body(e))
    except ValueError:
        return False
    if not isinstance(doc, dict):
        return False
    details = doc.get("details") if isinstance(doc.get("details"), dict) else {}
    return CAP_CODE in (details.get("code"), doc.get("code"))


def http_reason(e):
    """`HTTP <code> <reason>` for an HTTPError: the body's error field, else the
    body, first 120 chars. Only the response is read, never the request headers."""
    raw = http_body(e)
    try:
        doc = json.loads(raw)
        text = doc["error"] if isinstance(doc, dict) and doc.get("error") else raw
    except ValueError:
        text = raw
    text = " ".join(str(text).split())[:120]
    return f"HTTP {e.code} {text}".rstrip()


def failure(e):
    """(text, HTTP status or None) for a failed write; never the key."""
    if isinstance(e, urllib.error.HTTPError):
        return http_reason(e), e.code
    return type(e).__name__, None


class Writer:
    """Every board write: paced by `gap` seconds, 429/503 retried with backoff.
    All waiting goes through `wait`, so a test can make it zero-length.
    Board issue writes are counted in `sent` (every attempt) and `ok` (accepted);
    one past `budget`, or the board's cap 429, raises Stop and is never retried.
    `reserve` is how many board issue writes the item still needs after this one
    (SOF-10912): an attempt, a retry included, is sent only when it and the
    reserve both fit, so a retry never spends the room its status write needs."""

    def __init__(self, board, wait, gap, budget=MAX_WRITES):
        self.board, self.wait, self.gap, self.last = board, wait, gap, None
        self.budget, self.sent, self.ok = budget, 0, 0

    def call(self, method, path, body, reserve=0):
        counted = path.startswith(ISSUE_WRITE)
        for attempt in range(ATTEMPTS):
            if counted and self.sent + 1 + reserve > self.budget:
                why = "" if not attempt else ": no room to retry a write and finish its item"
                raise Stop(f"write budget of {self.budget} spent{why}", "budget")
            if self.last is not None:
                self.wait(max(0.0, self.gap - (time.monotonic() - self.last)))
            self.last = time.monotonic()
            if counted:
                self.sent += 1
            try:
                out = self.board.call(method, path, body)
                if counted:
                    self.ok += 1
                return out
            except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:
                if is_cap(e):
                    raise Stop(f"cross-issue write cap reached: {http_reason(e)}", "cap")
                if e.code not in RETRY_STATUS or attempt == ATTEMPTS - 1:
                    raise
                try:
                    delay = min(float(e.headers.get("Retry-After")), RETRY_AFTER_CAP)
                except (TypeError, ValueError):
                    delay = float(2 ** attempt)
                self.wait(max(0.0, delay))


def bget(board, path):
    try:
        return board.call("GET", path)
    except Exception as e:  # never echo the key or the body
        die(f"board GET {path.split('?')[0]} failed: {type(e).__name__}")


def paged(board, path):
    """Every issue a list path returns, deduplicated by id across pages."""
    seen, out = set(), []
    sep = "&" if "?" in path else "?"
    for page in range(MAX_PAGES):
        items = bget(board, f"{path}{sep}limit={PAGE}&offset={page * PAGE}")
        if not isinstance(items, list):
            die(f"board {path.split('?')[0]} did not return a list")
        for it in items:
            if it.get("id") not in seen:
                seen.add(it.get("id"))
                out.append(it)
        if len(items) < PAGE:
            return out
    die(f"board {path.split('?')[0]} has more than {MAX_PAGES} pages")


def when(stamp):
    """An ISO-8601 stamp as an aware datetime; Forge and the board use different offsets."""
    return datetime.datetime.fromisoformat(stamp.replace("Z", "+00:00"))


def newest(issues):
    return max(issues, key=lambda i: (i.get("createdAt") or "", i.get("identifier") or ""))


def main(argv):
    apply, base, forge_url, i = False, None, None, 0
    while i < len(argv):
        a = argv[i]
        if a == "--apply":
            apply, i = True, i + 1
        elif a in ("--base-url", "--forge-url"):
            if i + 1 >= len(argv):
                die(f"{a} needs a value", 2)
            if a == "--base-url":
                base = argv[i + 1]
            else:
                forge_url = argv[i + 1]
            i += 2
        else:
            die("usage: board-sweep [--apply] [--base-url URL] [--forge-url URL]", 2)
    board_url = (base or os.environ.get("PAPERCLIP_API_URL", "")).rstrip("/")
    forge_api = (forge_url or os.environ.get("FORGEJO_API_URL", "")).rstrip("/")
    key = os.environ.get("PAPERCLIP_API_KEY", "")
    company = os.environ.get("PAPERCLIP_COMPANY_ID", "")
    token = os.environ.get("FORGEJO_TOKEN", "")
    run_id = os.environ.get("PAPERCLIP_RUN_ID", "")
    if not (board_url and forge_api and key and company and token):
        die("PAPERCLIP_API_URL, PAPERCLIP_API_KEY, PAPERCLIP_COMPANY_ID, FORGEJO_TOKEN and "
            "FORGEJO_API_URL are required (or --base-url / --forge-url)", 3)
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[\w-]+", company) or (run_id and not re.fullmatch(r"[\w-]+", run_id)):
        die("PAPERCLIP_COMPANY_ID and PAPERCLIP_RUN_ID must be ids", 2)
    board = Http(board_url, f"Bearer {key}", run_id)
    wait = (lambda s: None) if os.environ.get("BOARD_SWEEP_NO_WAIT") == "1" else time.sleep
    try:
        gap = int(os.environ.get("BOARD_SWEEP_WRITE_GAP_MS", "200")) / 1000
    except ValueError:
        die("BOARD_SWEEP_WRITE_GAP_MS must be an integer", 2)
    try:
        stall_min = int(os.environ.get("BOARD_SWEEP_STALL_MIN", "30"))
    except ValueError:
        die("BOARD_SWEEP_STALL_MIN must be an integer", 2)
    try:
        budget = int(os.environ.get("BOARD_SWEEP_MAX_WRITES", str(MAX_WRITES)))
        if budget < 0:
            raise ValueError
    except ValueError:
        die("BOARD_SWEEP_MAX_WRITES must be a whole number", 2)
    try:
        now = when(os.environ["BOARD_SWEEP_NOW"]) if os.environ.get("BOARD_SWEEP_NOW") else \
            datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc)
    except ValueError:
        die("BOARD_SWEEP_NOW must be an ISO-8601 time", 2)
    writer = Writer(board, wait, gap, budget)
    forge = Http(forge_api, f"token {token}")
    cpath = f"/api/companies/{company}"

    agents = bget(board, f"{cpath}/agents")
    agents = agents if isinstance(agents, list) else []
    names = {a.get("id"): a.get("name") for a in agents}
    nag = [a.get("id") for a in agents if a.get("name") == NAGATHA and a.get("id")]
    if len(nag) != 1:
        die(f"board has {len(nag)} agents named {NAGATHA}, need exactly 1")
    bishop = [a.get("id") for a in agents if a.get("name") == ESCALATE_TO and a.get("id")]
    slots = {}
    for a in agents:
        n = ((a.get("runtimeConfig") or {}).get("heartbeat") or {}).get("maxConcurrentRuns")
        slots[a.get("id")] = n if isinstance(n, int) and n > 0 else 1
    blocked = paged(board, f"{cpath}/issues?status=blocked")
    everything = paged(board, f"{cpath}/issues")
    by_id = {it.get("id"): it for it in everything}
    for it in blocked:
        by_id.setdefault(it.get("id"), it)
    open_issues = [it for it in by_id.values() if it.get("status") not in TERMINAL]
    children = {}
    for it in by_id.values():
        if it.get("parentId"):
            children.setdefault(it["parentId"], []).append(it)

    prs, authors, errors = {}, {}, 0
    merge_rules = runpy.run_path(str(Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2] / "merge-pr/bin/merge-check"))
    # Capacity reads live-runs (queued and running only, at most LIVE_RUNS_CAP
    # rows): exact below the cap, at least the cap when it is full, so free
    # slots fail closed. heartbeat-runs is a window that mixes finished runs and
    # misses active ones; it is not read. A failed read holds every kickstart
    # and release this sweep.
    hold, busy, busy_floor = "", {}, 0
    try:
        live = board.call("GET", f"{cpath}/live-runs")
        if not isinstance(live, list):
            raise ValueError("live-runs not a list")
        for r in live:
            busy[(r or {}).get("agentId")] = busy.get((r or {}).get("agentId"), 0) + 1
        busy_floor = LIVE_RUNS_CAP if len(live) >= LIVE_RUNS_CAP else 0
    except Exception as e:
        errors += 1
        hold = f"board GET live-runs failed: {failure(e)[0]}"
        sys.stderr.write(f"board-sweep: {hold}\n")

    def pr_state(repo, num):
        """'open:<sha>', 'merged', 'closed', or None when the read failed."""
        k = f"{repo}#{num}"
        if k not in prs:
            try:
                pr = forge.call("GET", f"/repos/{urllib.parse.quote(repo, safe='/')}/pulls/{num}")
                authors[k] = (pr.get("user") or {}).get("login") or ""
                if pr.get("merged"):
                    prs[k] = "merged"
                elif pr.get("state") != "open":
                    prs[k] = "closed"
                else:
                    prs[k] = "open:" + ((pr.get("head") or {}).get("sha") or "")
            except Exception as e:
                prs[k] = None
                sys.stderr.write(f"board-sweep: forge GET {k} failed: {type(e).__name__}\n")
        return prs[k]

    checks = {}

    def failed_check(repo, sha):
        """The first required check at failure|error on sha, '' when none, None when the read failed."""
        k = f"{repo}@{sha}"
        if k not in checks:
            try:
                doc = forge.call("GET", f"/repos/{urllib.parse.quote(repo, safe='/')}/commits/{sha}/status")
                states = {s.get("context"): s.get("status") or s.get("state")
                          for s in ((doc or {}).get("statuses") or [])}
                checks[k] = next((c for c in REQUIRED_CHECKS if states.get(c) in ("failure", "error")), "")
            except Exception as e:
                checks[k] = None
                sys.stderr.write(f"board-sweep: forge GET {repo}@{sha[:7]} status failed: {type(e).__name__}\n")
        return checks[k]

    verdicts = {}

    def lead_verdict(group):
        """Use the merge gate's exact-head authority and precedence rules."""
        if group not in verdicts:
            repo, num, sha7 = group
            try:
                verdict, ev, _ = merge_rules["review_verdict"](
                    board_url, key, company, repo, num, prs[f"{repo}#{num}"][5:],
                    authors[f"{repo}#{num}"])
                verdicts[group] = (verdict or "") if not ev["held"] else ""
            except (Exception, SystemExit) as e:
                verdicts[group] = None
                sys.stderr.write(f"board-sweep: authoritative review for {repo}#{num} @ {sha7} failed: "
                                 f"{type(e).__name__}\n")
        return verdicts[group]

    kickbacks = {}  # issue id -> (repo, num, sha7) for the Forge comment

    def invalid(it, m):
        """(action, reason) when the review is not worth running, None when it is valid."""
        nonlocal errors
        st = pr_state(m.group(1), m.group(2))
        if st is None:
            errors += 1
            return ("other", "PR read failed")
        if st in ("merged", "closed"):
            return ("cancel", f"PR {st}")
        if not st[5:].startswith(m.group(3)):
            return ("cancel", f"head moved to {st[5:12]}")
        key = (m.group(1), m.group(2), m.group(3)[:7])
        said = lead_verdict(key)
        if said is None:
            errors += 1
            return ("other", "comment read failed")
        bad = failed_check(m.group(1), st[5:])
        if bad is None:
            errors += 1
            return ("other", "check read failed")
        if bad:
            sha7 = m.group(3)[:7]
            kickbacks[it.get("id")] = (m.group(1), m.group(2), sha7)
            return ("kickback", f"{bad} failed at {sha7}: the author fixes it and pushes; "
                                "a new head gets a new review")
        if said == "fix-first":
            kickbacks[it.get("id")] = key
            return ("kickback", f"verdict fix-first at {key[2]}: the author fixes the findings and "
                                "pushes; a new head gets a new review")
        return None

    plan = {}  # issue id -> (action, reason)
    reviews = {}  # exact title -> [issues still in play]
    for it in blocked:
        iid, title = it.get("id"), it.get("title") or ""
        if it.get("assigneeAgentId") == nag[0]:
            plan[iid] = ("nagatha", "Nagatha's task")
            continue
        m = REVIEW.match(title)
        if m:
            verdict = invalid(it, m)
            if verdict:
                plan[iid] = verdict
            else:
                reviews.setdefault(title, []).append(it)
            continue
        m = FOLLOW_UP.match(title)
        if m:
            st = pr_state(m.group(1), m.group(2))
            if st is None:
                errors += 1
                plan[iid] = ("other", "PR read failed")
            elif st in ("merged", "closed"):
                plan[iid] = ("cancel", f"PR {st}")
            else:
                plan[iid] = ("merge-check", "PR open; merge-check owns it")
            continue
        if it.get("originKind") == "routine_execution" and it.get("originId"):
            peers = [o for o in open_issues
                     if o.get("originKind") == "routine_execution" and o.get("originId") == it["originId"]]
            top = newest(peers + [it])
            if top.get("id") == iid:
                plan[iid] = ("routine-kept", "newest open instance of its routine")
            else:
                plan[iid] = ("cancel", f"one open instance per routine; newest is {top.get('identifier')}")
            continue
        kids = children.get(iid, [])
        if kids and all(k.get("status") in TERMINAL for k in kids):
            # Finished children are not enough (SOF-10842): a live first-class
            # blocker keeps the parent blocked. Only the detail read carries
            # blockedBy, and only a done blocker is resolved.
            try:
                detail = board.call("GET", f"/api/issues/{urllib.parse.quote(str(iid), safe='')}")
                deps = (detail or {}).get("blockedBy") if isinstance(detail, dict) else None
                if not isinstance(deps, list):
                    raise ValueError("issue detail has no blockedBy list")
            except Exception as e:
                errors += 1
                plan[iid] = ("other", "children finished; blocker read failed")
                sys.stderr.write(f"board-sweep: board GET detail for {it.get('identifier')} failed: "
                                 f"{e if isinstance(e, ValueError) else failure(e)[0]}\n")
                continue
            live = [d if isinstance(d, dict) else {} for d in deps]
            live = [d for d in live if d.get("status") != "done"]
            if live:
                named = ", ".join(f"{d.get('identifier') or d.get('id') or '?'} ({d.get('status') or 'unknown'})"
                                  for d in live)
                plan[iid] = ("other", f"children finished; blocked by {named}")
                continue
            plan[iid] = ("todo", "all children finished")
            continue
        m = TRIAGE.match(title)
        if m:
            ipath = f"/repos/{urllib.parse.quote(m.group(1), safe='/')}/issues/{m.group(2)}"
            try:
                fi = forge.call("GET", ipath)
                comments = forge.call("GET", f"{ipath}/comments") or []
            except Exception as e:
                errors += 1
                plan[iid] = ("other", "issue read failed")
                sys.stderr.write(f"board-sweep: forge GET {m.group(1)}#{m.group(2)} failed: "
                                 f"{type(e).__name__}\n")
                continue
            if fi.get("state") != "open":
                plan[iid] = ("cancel", "issue closed")
                continue
            author = (fi.get("user") or {}).get("login")
            since = it.get("updatedAt") or ""
            replies = [c.get("created_at") for c in comments
                       if author and (c.get("user") or {}).get("login") == author and c.get("created_at")]
            last = max(replies, key=when, default=None)
            if last and since and when(last) > when(since):
                plan[iid] = ("todo", f"author replied {last}")
            else:
                plan[iid] = ("waiting-author", f"no author reply since {since}")
            continue
        plan[iid] = ("other", "no rule matched")
    candidates = []  # (issue, action, reason): each one would set the task todo
    for group in reviews.values():
        top = newest(group)
        candidates.append((top, "todo", "newest review for the live head"))
        for it in group:
            if it is not top:
                plan[it["id"]] = ("cancel", f"superseded by {top.get('identifier')}")

    # Reviews already in todo or in_progress: kick back the invalid, kickstart
    # the stalled. A blocked review waits on its children; those are checked.
    escalations = {}  # issue id -> title of the Bishop issue to open
    open_titles = {o.get("title"): o.get("identifier") for o in open_issues}
    active = [it for it in by_id.values()
              if it.get("status") in ("todo", "in_progress", "backlog") and REVIEW.match(it.get("title") or "")
              and it.get("assigneeAgentId") != nag[0]]
    for it in active:
        iid, title = it.get("id"), it.get("title") or ""
        verdict = invalid(it, REVIEW.match(title))
        if verdict:
            plan[iid] = verdict
            continue
        if it.get("status") == "backlog":
            # The queue: a review waiting its turn is backlog, never blocked.
            candidates.append((it, "todo", "released from the queue"))
            continue
        since = it.get("updatedAt")
        if not since:
            continue
        idle = (now - when(since)).total_seconds() / 60
        if idle <= stall_min:
            continue
        q = urllib.parse.quote(str(iid), safe="")
        try:
            own = board.call("GET", f"/api/issues/{q}/runs")
            if not isinstance(own, list):
                raise ValueError("runs not a list")
        except Exception as e:
            errors += 1
            plan[iid] = ("other", "run read failed")
            why = f"board GET runs for {it.get('identifier')} failed: {failure(e)[0]}"
            hold = hold or why
            sys.stderr.write(f"board-sweep: {why}\n")
            continue
        if any((r or {}).get("status") in ACTIVE_RUN for r in own):
            continue
        try:
            notes = board.call("GET", f"/api/issues/{urllib.parse.quote(str(iid), safe='')}/comments")
            if not isinstance(notes, list):
                raise ValueError("comments not a list")
        except Exception as e:
            errors += 1
            plan[iid] = ("other", "comment read failed")
            sys.stderr.write(f"board-sweep: board GET comments for {it.get('identifier')} failed: "
                             f"{type(e).__name__}\n")
            continue
        # Only restarts the board accepted count: a refused PATCH leaves a
        # KICKSTART_REFUSED note that cancels its kickstart comment.
        bodies = [str((c or {}).get("body") or "") for c in notes]
        kicks = sum(1 for b in bodies if b.startswith(f"{KICKSTART} -- ")) - \
            sum(1 for b in bodies if b.startswith(KICKSTART_REFUSED))
        if kicks >= KICKSTARTS_BEFORE_ESCALATE:
            etitle = f"Stalled review: {title}"
            if etitle in open_titles:
                plan[iid] = ("escalate", f"already escalated: {open_titles[etitle]}")
            else:
                plan[iid] = ("escalate", "stalled after two kickstarts")
                escalations[iid] = etitle
            continue
        candidates.append((it, "kickstart",
                           f"{it.get('status')}, no queued or running run, idle {int(idle)} min"))

    # The crew is finite (The operator, 2026-10-04): the most important first, the
    # rest wait in the queue. Setting todo wakes the assignee, so each one
    # takes at most its free run slots this pass.
    def rank(it):
        pri = str(it.get("priority") or "").lower()
        nums = []
        for lb in it.get("labels") or []:
            hit = PRI_LABEL.match(str((lb or {}).get("name") or "")) if isinstance(lb, dict) else None
            if hit:
                nums.append(int(hit.group(1)))
        return (PRIORITY.index(pri) if pri in PRIORITY else len(PRIORITY),
                min(nums) if nums else sys.maxsize, it.get("createdAt") or "")

    candidates.sort(key=lambda c: rank(c[0]))
    taken, nudged, waiting = {}, set(), []
    for it, action, reason in candidates:
        if hold:
            plan[it["id"]] = ("other", f"not released: {hold}")
            continue
        who = it.get("assigneeAgentId")
        free = max(0, slots.get(who, 1) - max(busy.get(who, 0), busy_floor))
        if not who or taken.get(who, 0) < free:
            taken[who] = taken.get(who, 0) + 1
            plan[it["id"]] = (action, reason)
        elif action == "kickstart" and free == 0 and who not in nudged:
            nudged.add(who)
            plan[it["id"]] = (action, reason)
        else:
            waiting.append(it)
    for k, it in enumerate(waiting, 1):
        # Waiting for a free reviewer is queued, not blocked (The operator, 2026-10-04:
        # the Blocked inbox holds only what is really stuck): a blocked one
        # moves to backlog, and later passes release it from there.
        plan[it["id"]] = ("queue" if it.get("status") == "blocked" else "review-next-pass",
                          f"queued: priority {it.get('priority') or 'none'}, position {k}")

    counts = {a: 0 for a in ACTIONS}
    items, error_codes, skipped = [], {}, 0

    def failed(item, what, e):
        nonlocal errors
        text, code = failure(e)
        errors += 1
        item["error"] = f"{what} failed: {text}"
        if code is not None:
            error_codes[str(code)] = error_codes.get(str(code), 0) + 1

    posted = set()  # (repo, num, sha7) kickbacks already on Forge this pass
    made = set()  # Bishop issue titles opened this pass
    spec_steps = {(it.get("originKind"), it.get("originId")) for it in by_id.values()}

    def forge_kickback(key, reason):
        """One `REVIEW KICKBACK:` comment per PR and sha7, skipped when Forge already has it."""
        if key in posted:
            return
        repo, num, sha7 = key
        cpath_f = f"/repos/{urllib.parse.quote(repo, safe='/')}/issues/{num}/comments"
        prior = forge.call("GET", cpath_f) or []
        if not any(str((c or {}).get("body") or "").startswith("REVIEW KICKBACK:")
                   and sha7 in str(c.get("body")) for c in prior):
            forge.call("POST", cpath_f, {"body": f"REVIEW KICKBACK: {reason}"})
        posted.add(key)

    def apply_item(it, item, action, reason):
        nonlocal skipped
        ipath = f"/api/issues/{urllib.parse.quote(str(it.get('id')), safe='')}"
        if apply and action == "escalate" and it.get("id") in escalations:
            etitle = escalations[it["id"]]
            if etitle not in made:
                made.add(etitle)
                try:
                    if len(bishop) != 1:
                        raise LookupError(f"{len(bishop)} agents named {ESCALATE_TO}")
                    writer.call("POST", f"{ipath}/comments", {"body": f"board-sweep: escalate -- {reason}"})
                    writer.call("POST", f"{cpath}/issues", {
                        "title": etitle, "priority": "high", "status": "todo",
                        "assigneeAgentId": bishop[0],
                        "description": (f"Review task {it.get('identifier')} ({it.get('title')}) stalled "
                                        f"after two board-sweep kickstarts with no progress. Assignee: "
                                        f"{names.get(it.get('assigneeAgentId'))}. Unstick it, reassign "
                                        "it, or cancel it with a reason.")})
                except Exception as e:
                    failed(item, "escalate", e)
        if apply and action == "kickback":
            try:
                forge_kickback(kickbacks[it["id"]], reason)
            except Exception as e:
                failed(item, "forge comment", e)
                return
        if apply and action in ("todo", "kickstart") and not (EXEMPT.match(it.get("title") or "") or REVIEW.match(it.get("title") or "") or re.match(r"^\s*(?:Checks not green: \S+/\S+#\d+ @ [0-9a-f]{7,40}|Resolve merge-check read failure(?: on|:)? \S+/\S+#\d+(?: @ [0-9a-f]{7,40})?)$", it.get("title") or "", re.I)):
            # A redispatch wakes paid work too: gate before either the comment
            # or status write. Keep spec-task writes on this sweep's Writer.
            try:
                result = subprocess.run(
                    [str(Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3] / "bin/spec-ready"),
                     "--task-json"],
                    input=json.dumps(it), text=True, capture_output=True, timeout=60)
                if result.returncode != 0:
                    skipped += 1
                    item["skipped"] = "spec-ready hold: write-spec"
                    if result.returncode == 1:
                        held = json.loads(result.stdout)
                        source = held.get("issueUrl") or str(it.get("id"))
                        body_hash = held["bodyHash"]
                        origin = ("spec-ready", f"{source}:{body_hash}")
                        if origin not in spec_steps:
                            writer.call("POST", f"{cpath}/issues", {
                                "title": f"Write spec {source}", "status": "backlog",
                                "assigneeAgentId": None, "originKind": origin[0], "originId": origin[1],
                                "description": (f"Source: {source}\nMissing: " +
                                                ", ".join(held["missing"]) +
                                                "\nWrite the missing spec before implementation dispatch.")})
                            spec_steps.add(origin)
                    else:
                        failed(item, "spec-ready", RuntimeError(result.stderr.strip() or "harness failed"))
                    return
            except Exception as e:
                skipped += 1
                item["skipped"] = "spec-ready hold: write-spec"
                failed(item, "spec-ready", e)
                return
        if apply and action in ("cancel", "todo", "kickstart", "kickback", "queue"):
            status = "todo" if action in ("todo", "kickstart") else "backlog" if action == "queue" else "cancelled"
            # After the comment: its PATCH, and a kickstart's possible refusal note.
            note = 1 if action == "kickstart" else 0
            try:
                writer.call("POST", f"{ipath}/comments", {"body": f"board-sweep: {action} -- {reason}"},
                            reserve=1 + note)
            except Exception as e:
                failed(item, "comment", e)
            else:
                try:
                    writer.call("PATCH", ipath, {"status": status}, reserve=note)
                except Stop as s:
                    if note and s.kind == "budget":
                        # The reserved room: the kickstart comment never counts as a restart.
                        try:
                            writer.call("POST", f"{ipath}/comments", {
                                "body": f"{KICKSTART_REFUSED} -- status not written: {s}"})
                        except Exception as e2:
                            failed(item, "refusal comment", e2)
                    raise
                except Exception as e:
                    if isinstance(e, urllib.error.HTTPError) and e.code == 422 and status == "todo":
                        skipped += 1
                        item["skipped"] = f"board refused todo: {http_reason(e)}"
                    else:
                        failed(item, "status", e)
                    if action == "kickstart":
                        # Not a restart: say so, so it never counts toward escalation.
                        try:
                            writer.call("POST", f"{ipath}/comments", {
                                "body": f"{KICKSTART_REFUSED} -- {item.get('skipped') or item.get('error')}"})
                        except Exception as e2:
                            failed(item, "refusal comment", e2)

    # Everything goes out in priority order within the write budget (SOF-10747);
    # within one priority, cleanups before releases, as before.
    queued_ids = {c[0].get("id") for c in candidates}
    order = [it for it in blocked + [a for a in active if a.get("id") in plan]
             if it.get("id") not in queued_ids] + [c[0] for c in candidates]
    order.sort(key=lambda it: rank(it)[:2] + (it.get("id") in queued_ids, it.get("createdAt") or ""))
    stopped, planned = None, 0

    def next_pass(item, action, reason, why):
        item.update(action="next-pass", planned=action, reason=f"{why}; planned {action} -- {reason}")
        counts["next-pass"] += 1

    for it in order:
        action, reason = plan[it.get("id")]
        item = {"identifier": it.get("identifier"), "title": it.get("title"), "action": action,
                "reason": reason, "assignee": names.get(it.get("assigneeAgentId"))}
        items.append(item)
        need = (1 if it.get("id") in escalations else 0) if action == "escalate" else COST.get(action, 0)
        if need and not stopped and (writer.sent if apply else planned) + need > budget:
            stopped = f"write budget of {budget} spent"
        if need and stopped:
            next_pass(item, action, reason, stopped.split(": ")[0])
            continue
        planned += need
        ok_before = writer.ok
        try:
            apply_item(it, item, action, reason)
        except Stop as s:
            stopped = str(s)
            next_pass(item, action, reason, stopped.split(": ")[0])
            n = writer.ok - ok_before
            if n:
                limit = "the cap" if s.kind == "cap" else "the write budget ran out"
                item["partial"] = f"{n} write{'s' if n != 1 else ''} went out before {limit}"
            continue
        counts[action] += 1
    if stopped:
        sys.stderr.write(f"board-sweep: {stopped}; {counts['next-pass']} items left for the next pass\n")

    out = {"mode": "apply" if apply else "dry-run", "blocked_before": len(blocked), "actions": counts,
           "errors": errors, "error_codes": error_codes, "skipped": skipped,
           "write_budget": budget, "writes": writer.sent, "stopped": stopped, "items": items,
           "queue": [{"identifier": it.get("identifier"), "priority": it.get("priority"),
                      "assignee": names.get(it.get("assigneeAgentId"))} for it in waiting[:QUEUE_SHOWN]]}
    if apply:
        out["blocked_after"] = len(paged(board, f"{cpath}/issues?status=blocked"))
    out["exit"] = 1 if errors else 0
    print(json.dumps(out))
    sys.exit(out["exit"])


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main(sys.argv[1:])
